1. Explain jenkins architecture 
  
   jenkins-controller
         "The Jenkins Controller is responsible for managing jobs, scheduling builds, maintaining configurations and coordinating agents."
         
    jenkins-agents 
        "Jenkins Agents execute build, testing and deployment tasks assigned by the Controller. They help distribute workloads and improve scalability."
        
2. What is an executor in Jenkins?
         An Executor is a slot on an agent or controller where a build can run.
         
         For example:

           If an agent has 2 executors, it can run up to 2 builds simultaneously, subject to available resources.   
           
