1. What is the difference between CMD and ENTRYPOINT?

    "ENTRYPOINT and CMD are Dockerfile instructions used to define container startup behavior. ENTRYPOINT specifies the main executable, whereas CMD provides default arguments or a default command. When both are used together, ENTRYPOINT executes the application and CMD provides default arguments, which can be overridden during container execution."

       ENTRYPOINT = Main executable.
       CMD = Default command or arguments.  

